Step builder
WorkflowNode is the base class that gives every builder job() and build(). StepBuilder describes one step. You rarely create one yourself: JobBuilder.step(name) makes it and adds it to the job.


source

WorkflowNode
def WorkflowNode(
    *args, **kwargs
):
Base class providing job() and build() navigation to all fluent builders.




source

StepBuilder
def StepBuilder(
    name:str, job
):
Fluent builder for a single workflow step.



Core step fields
A step does one of two things. run gives it a shell command, and uses names an action to run instead, with with_ supplying the action’s inputs. The other methods set optional fields. env adds environment variables, id names the step so later steps can read its outputs, if_ runs it only when a condition holds, continue_on_error lets the job carry on when the step fails, timeout_minutes limits how long it may take, and working_directory sets the folder a run command starts in. if_ and with_ end in an underscore because if and with are Python keywords.


